      "content": "Here's an explanation of mitosis suitable for high schoolers: \n\nMitosis is the process by which a cell divides into two identical daughter cells, ensuring that the offspring inherits the same amount of genetic material as the parent cell. During mitosis, the replicated DNA unwinds and the nuclear envelope disintegrates, allowing the duplicated chromosomes to condense and align at the center of the cell. A member cell or pair of sister cell divides into two new cells: a daughter cell and another daughter cell that's genetically identical. This replication process is crucial for growth and repair of tissues in our bodies, as it occurs at an incredible rate to replace old or damaged cells.",
